1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,928
Doing everything right for stronger nails, but they still split at the tip, grow in thinner, or pick up ridges anyway?

2
00:00:06,248 --> 00:00:09,731
Three things you drink or eat most days could be working against you.

3
00:00:10,051 --> 00:00:15,861
Nails are built almost entirely from keratin, a protein - and several nutrients help your body produce it.

4
00:00:16,181 --> 00:00:18,468
A few common food and drink habits get in the way.

5
00:00:18,788 --> 00:00:27,897
Drinking wine or beer often can interfere with how your body absorbs and stores biotin - the nutrient your nail cells rely on most to build keratin.

6
00:00:28,217 --> 00:00:38,561
Coffee's caffeine has a diuretic effect, and separately, compounds in coffee can reduce how much iron and zinc your gut absorbs from meals - both minerals nails need to grow strong.

7
00:00:38,881 --> 00:00:48,108
Instant ramen and other packaged snacks are filling but nutrient-poor, so eating them often can leave you short on the protein and minerals nails are actually built from.

8
00:00:48,428 --> 00:00:55,867
Try alternating alcohol with water and cutting back overall, and space coffee out from mealtimes so it doesn't compete with nutrient absorption.

9
00:00:56,187 --> 00:01:00,774
Swapping in more eggs or beans instead of instant noodles can help too.
